A||N||6||Ozzy||New Rims... What tires??||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||02-17-2000||12:59 AM||||Hi Gang.<P>Just bought some rims from a guy on E-Bay. They are 15 x 6. What is the widest tire I can fit safely on this size rim??<P>Ozzy||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-17-2000||08:55 AM||||you can cram a 245 on their but that will leave almost 2 full inches unsupported by the wheel! a 225 would be safer leaving only 1.5" unsupported.  (225/25.4-6/2=1.49") and teh size of the tire may throw off the speedo by only 1 mph@100mph  (width*aspect ratio/25.4)(x2+wheel diameter=diameter of tire)   225*.50/25.4=4.429*2=8.85+15=23.85 then divid that by the factory #of 23.68 = 1.007179 miles per hour off @ 100. So a SWEET tire is a Yokohama AVS imtermediate or an A509. they have a treadwear of 140 and will be pretty hard pressed to break loose! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-17-2000||08:56 AM||||sorry for the math lesson just wanted you to see how i came up with my information... I have a set of A509s on my stockys and AVS Intermediates on my Alfa Romeo 164L... love everyminute of both sets!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||02-18-2000||02:34 AM||||I'm running 225/50-16 all around with just a little understeer.  Looking at the numbers it would seem dropping to a 205/50-15 would lower the front almost an inch.  Any idea if this would really pissoff my low speed understeer?<BR>The wheels ar 16x7 and 15x6, I like the look of straight up and down sidewalls<p>[This message has been edited by Phaeton (edited 02-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||02-18-2000||10:50 PM||||Phaeton,a taller sidewall will give you a little more slip angle(range of grip),so a taller tire in front will help the understeer,maybe a 195/60-15.Since these cars oversteer in extreme conditions,I tend to go firmer and wider in back,like you've done.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||02-19-2000||12:15 AM||||Food for thought, gotta do something, the 16's on the front 'feel' like they're fighting with themselves when going fairly straight and feel good only on hard cornering.<BR>Trying to avoid making the understeer worse with the fix though.<BR>Thanx for input. ||||reg||14
Z||000006||Ozzy||02-19-2000||02:45 AM||||So I'm wondering about a set of BFG TA's, like 215/60/15. I put a set of Centenial 215/60/14's all around from the other car and the driving difference was so dramatic from the 195/60/14's I had on it, that it felt like driving a different car!<P>Hey Low CG...have not seen you post for awhile. We still have to get together sometime. I'm in Port Orchard just up the road from u. I tried to e-mail you but some other dude responded??<P>Ozzy||||reg||5
